  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-06-14T12:54:37.681Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am using the latest version of VRChat on Steam. This did not used to happen with previous versions, but ever since the last two updates. At completely random times, with no visible reason, and regardless of connection to server, people present, or any other factors that would contribute to an FPS drop, the FPS severely drops, to roughly 11FPS, and stays that way for an unspecified amount of time, not only making the game unplayable, but furthermore sound also cuts out, and all you can hear is small tidbits of glitched conversation. Sometimes the FPS goes back up, however then all characters freeze and only one person can be heard talking. Leaving the world and rejoining does not help. After this bug happened almost 5 times in the period of an hour, I found this to be ridiculous and decided to post this. It would be much appreciated if the team could find out the reason for this and patch it as soon as possible, since it is not only making the game unplayable, but also interfering with my conversations with my dear friends.",
